{
  "Date": "05/09/2026",
  "Title": "Rising Dam Levels Across India ",
  "Category": "GS I - Geography | GS II - Governance | GS III - Environment",
  "Banner_Image": "https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=14Ykp4WDyKbZy3GtNrVT0L4dwYgcU5BOc&sz=w1200",
  "Short_Summary": "India’s reservoir storage shows regional gains despite deficient monsoon rainfall, highlighting water availability, irrigation needs, regional disparities, and the importance of sustainable reservoir management.",
  "Full_Content": "<p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>Syllabus Areas:</strong></p><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\">GS I - Geography</p><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\">GS II - Governance</p><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\">GS III - Environment</p><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\">India’s reservoir storage is in focus amid a deficient monsoon, with Central and Western regions exceeding 80% capacity, while overall storage remains below last year’s level and the 10-year average. </p><h4 class=\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mt-5 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>Also Read: </strong><a href=\"https://egurukulamforias.com/current-affairs/jal-sanchay-jan-bhagidari-jsjb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#6C1D18] font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 decoration-[#6C1D18]/40 hover:decoration-[#6C1D18] transition-colors\"><strong>Jal Sanchay Jan Bhagidari (JSJB)</strong></a></h4><h4 class=\"text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mt-5 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>What is a Reservoir?</strong></h4><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\">A <strong>reservoir is a large, artificial or natural storage area used to collect and store water</strong>, usually created by building a <strong>dam across a river</strong>.</p><div class=\"my-8 text-left\"><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1TwPBFguxzXJgcrR6L8S8DqTh4BAhctBa&sz=w1200\" alt=\"Article Illustration\" class=\"rounded-2xl shadow-lg max-w-full inline-block\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></div><div class=\"my-8 text-left\"><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1FmfRsuWmhI10dsN20WuVKYeMqUs_wqeD&sz=w1200\" alt=\"Article Illustration\" class=\"rounded-2xl shadow-lg max-w-full inline-block\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></div><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>30%+ of 166 major reservoirs</strong> have storage above <strong>80% of capacity</strong>.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>South-West monsoon was 13% deficient</strong> as of September 3.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>47% of 734 districts</strong> received deficient rainfall.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>13 reservoirs were full</strong>, including <strong>5 in Maharashtra</strong>; <strong>51 remained below 50%</strong> capacity.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Continued rainfall in the coming days may <strong>further improve reservoir storage</strong>.</li><div class=\"my-8 text-left\"><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1r1vv5v8kS-9u363ENNdD_bKdig1WEkY2&sz=w1200\" alt=\"Article Illustration\" class=\"rounded-2xl shadow-lg max-w-full inline-block\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></div><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Central (81.2%) and Western (80.4%) regions</strong> recorded the highest storage levels.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Overall reservoir storage stood at <strong>56.76%</strong>, or <strong>129.87 BCM</strong> of 183.565 BCM capacity.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>4 of 5 regions</strong> had storage above <strong>60%</strong>, but Southern storage declined.</li><li class=\"ml-4 md:ml-6 pl-2 list-disc text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\">Overall storage remained <strong>below both last year’s level and the 10-year average</strong>.</li><div class=\"my-8 text-left\"><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1ydKcR_veZyWzApOmv3NfKvSxBaL1uvu9&sz=w1200\" alt=\"Article Illustration\" class=\"rounded-2xl shadow-lg max-w-full inline-block\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></div><div class=\"my-8 text-left\"><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1CvKgT-EkFYzgeXGu-ahgbViF1ZyMB9YI&sz=w1200\" alt=\"Article Illustration\" class=\"rounded-2xl shadow-lg max-w-full inline-block\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div>",
